   $q$Solve the system $x^2 + y^2 = 25$ and $x + y = 7$:$q$, $q$[{"text":"$(3, 4)$, $(4, 3)$, $(-3, -4)$ and $(-4, -3)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"included-circle-points-not-on-line"},{"text":"$(-3, 10)$ and $(-4, 11)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-factoring"},{"text":"$(3, 4)$ and $(4, 3)$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$(3, 4)$ only","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"kept-only-one-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$(3, 4)$ and $(4, 3)$$q$, $q$Write $y = 7 - x$ and substitute: $x^2 + 49 - 14x + x^2 = 25$, so $2x^2 - 14x + 24 = 0$, or $(x - 3)(x - 4) = 0$. Then $x = 3$ gives $y = 4$ and $x = 4$ gives $y = 3$, so the solutions are $(3, 4)$ and $(4, 3)$. The points $(-3, -4)$ and $(-4, -3)$ are on the circle, but their coordinates add to $-7$, not $7$.$q$, 'draft', null)
