   $q$Solve the system $y = x^2 - 2x - 3$ and $y = -x + 3$:$q$, $q$[{"text":"$(3, 0)$ and $(-2, 5)$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$(-3, 6)$ and $(2, 1)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-factoring"},{"text":"$(3, 0)$ and $(-2, -5)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dropped-sign-on-y"},{"text":"$(3, 0)$ only","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"kept-only-positive-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$(3, 0)$ and $(-2, 5)$$q$, $q$Set $x^2 - 2x - 3 = -x + 3$, so $x^2 - x - 6 = 0$, or $(x - 3)(x + 2) = 0$. Then $x = 3$ gives $y = 0$ and $x = -2$ gives $y = -(-2) + 3 = 5$. Both $(3, 0)$ and $(-2, 5)$ are solutions. The point $(-2, -5)$ loses the sign when computing $-(-2)$.$q$, 'draft', null)
